svg.desc:
Write. Fix. Reveal.
An authored source-editing demonstration with a resolved build-error transcript and a real chart outcome.

1. 01  Write the example
   C# source
   Language: csharp
   var chart = Chart.Create()
       .WithTitle("Build results")
       .WithXLabels("Mon", "Tue", "Wed")
       .AddBars("Passed", new[] {
           new ChartPoint(1, 12),
           new ChartPoint(2, 18),
           new ChartPoint(3, 24)
       });
   chart.SavePng("builds.png");

2. 02  Read the build error
   Language: csharp
   var chart = Chart.Create()
       .WithTitle("Build results")
       .WithXLabels("Mon", "Tue", "Wed")
       .AddBars("Passed", new[] {
           new ChartPoint(1, 12),
           new ChartPoint(2, 18),
           new ChartPoint(3, 24)
       });
   chart.SavePng("builds.png");
   [dotnet run] PS C:\> dotnet run
   [dotnet run] error CS1061: Chart has no
   [dotnet run] method named 'AddBars'.

3. 03  Correct the method
   Correct the method name
   Language: csharp
   var chart = Chart.Create()
       .WithTitle("Build results")
       .WithXLabels("Mon", "Tue", "Wed")
       .AddBar("Passed", new[] {
           new ChartPoint(1, 12),
           new ChartPoint(2, 18),
           new ChartPoint(3, 24)
       });
   chart.SavePng("builds.png");

4. 04  Run the corrected source
   Language: csharp
   var chart = Chart.Create()
       .WithTitle("Build results")
       .WithXLabels("Mon", "Tue", "Wed")
       .AddBar("Passed", new[] {
           new ChartPoint(1, 12),
           new ChartPoint(2, 18),
           new ChartPoint(3, 24)
       });
   chart.SavePng("builds.png");
   [dotnet run] PS C:\> dotnet run
   [dotnet run] Saved builds.png

5. 05  See the chart
   Passed builds: Monday 12, Tuesday 18, Wednesday 24.

Outcomes:
- builds.png
